  "note": "Private test build asked by the maintainer on the verified 835, after every Switch 2 game ran slower than real time on IPA 834 (Mario Kart World 62 to 90.5 % of real time, Zelda 25 to 49 %): the S2Arm engine with patch 0351 (pin 7df424f4, run 45449520140): the no-lock guard of 0319/0327/0344 and the trial of 0309 off for every game, the fallback to 30 of 0349 opt-in, the [rb-speed] measurement line; S2A_RB_NO_LOCK_GUARD=1 S2A_RB_DRS_TRIAL=1 S2A_RB_FALLBACK30=1 bring back 0350's behaviour. Everything else is the 835's: the MeloNX Core and its dependencies, the libretro collection LibretroCores-e5378e84 (DeSmuME and Azahar of the 835), RPCS3, Dolphin, ARMSX2, Xenia and NS2Pro unchanged. Source only, for a later build: the MoltenVK tenth part for MeloNX (1d413b0a and its pin a5b08812, with 3a18f778 the 835 left source only) and Azahar's tiled-GPU render passes (fceead82, 85a5528e). Device measurement pending.",
